ffers PyroThin aerogel thermal barriers for use in battery packs in EVs; Pyrogel XTE for refineries and petrochemical facilities; Pyrogel HPS for high temperatures and in demanding thermal applications in refining and chemical processing systems; Pyrogel XTF for protection against fire; Cryogel Z for sub-ambient and cryogenic applications; Spaceloft Subsea for pipe-in-pipe applications in offshore oil production; and Cryogel X201 for cold system designs. It serves EV manufacturers, automotive suppliers, lithium-ion battery manufacturers, and e-mobility and energy storage companies. The company was founded in 2001 and is headquartered in Northborough, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Donald R. Young | President, CEO & Director | Age 68 | Compensation: $589,365 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 854 people. Revenue per employee of $317K ranks in the bottom quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Aspen Aerogels, Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $464M market cap on $271M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -57% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $5M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -31.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Sha